  abstract: |
    Public and technical debate often sorts AI systems into "safe" and "dangerous."
    This paper argues the locus of risk and value is inferential: AI produces probabilistic
    inferences, not authority. We propose the Pilot Model with three levers (context,
    verification, bounded impact) and testable hypotheses.
